;
WELCOME MESSAGE AND HELP MAINTENANCE

A - Making the system your own

:A
MAKING THE SYSTEM YOUR OWN

The sign-on message should tell the caller where he's arrived and what he
might find there. A few lines are often sufficient; regular callers needn't
read several screens of announcements every time.

From private CP/M:

    SYSUTLS:ZDE A0:WELCOME.TXT

ZDE uses WordStar keys: Ctrl-K S saves, Ctrl-K X saves and exits, Ctrl-K Q
abandons changes. If an unchanged buffer prompts after a previous save, N
exits without saving again. Keep the caller blanked throughout editing and
saving. BYE displays WELCOME.TXT on the next call, not its .BAK file.

The HELP topics are in I14:HELP. DIR HELP: lists them; HELP GAMES opens a
particular topic. HELP topics use ASCII, a semicolon on the first line, CRLF
and Ctrl-Z termination. Keep lines within 78 characters and menu indexes
within one screen. Link to another topic with :A:HELP:TOPIC.HLP, or begin an
information section with :A on a line of its own. HELPC paginates long
information sections automatically. Maintain HELP privately, and put no
passwords or installation-specific secrets in public topics.
